**Theorem 4.3 (An active splitting event at every stationary optimum).**
Every stationary legal complex scalar port $S$ attaining the original
$\varepsilon_1$ satisfies

$$
\max_{J\in\mathcal J_{\rm split}}\|H_J(S)\|_{\rm op}
=\varepsilon_1.
\tag{4.11}
$$

In QRC's selected real reflected class, an optimum has at least one
of the following pairs of active events:

$$
(\{2\},\{5\}),\quad(\{N,2\},\{N,5\}),\quad
(\{2,3\},\{3,5\}),\quad(\{2,25\},\{5,25\}).
\tag{4.12}
$$

Proof. The credited bounds give
$1/2<L_*\le\varepsilon_1\le\lambda_Q<b_*$.
Suppose instead
$m=\max_{\mathcal J_{\rm split}}\|H_J(S)\|<\varepsilon_1$.
Concatenating scaled finite rank-one Kraus families makes
$S_t=(1-t)S+t\mathcal B$ a legal scalar port; it is stationary.
For every keep event its norm is at most
$(1-t)\varepsilon_1+t/2<\varepsilon_1$.
For every split event it is at most
$(1-t)m+tb_*<\varepsilon_1$ whenever

$$
0<t<\frac{\varepsilon_1-m}{b_*-m}.
\tag{4.13}
$$

The denominator is positive and this interval lies in $(0,1)$.
All fifteen constraints refer to this same channel, contradicting
optimality through (1.8). This proves (4.11) without reality or
reflection assumptions on the stationary optimum.

Let $W$ exchange modes $2,5$. It equals $P-R_0$, acts by $-1$ on
the dark line and by $1$ on the bright space. In QRC's complete
commutant coordinates it fixes the three invariant $H_i$, acts as
$-I$ on each dark/bright plane, and as $I$ on each bright/bright
plane. Thus every selected channel, including arbitrary nonsymmetric
population matrix $M$, commutes with $\operatorname{Ad}_W$.
Its adjoint does too, and
$H_{WJ}(S)=WH_J(S)W^T$. Each splitting event therefore has the
equally active partner in (4.12).
QPC supplies stationary optimizers for the entire original class;
QRC supplies selected representatives at the same value. The statement
does not assert zero-wait activity for every nonstationary optimizer
or determine which pair and signed eigenspaces are active. $\square$

